    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 1973-03-23; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Well; weight 63.4 kg; blood pressure 114/72, pulse 76</td></tr><tr><td>Cranial nerves</td><td>Normal; no nystagmus; visual acuity and fields normal</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Reduced vibration and joint position sense in the fingers of both hands, worse on the left, with mild wandering of the left fingers when the eyes are closed; light touch reduced in the fingertips; finger and wrist strength 5 out of 5 except finger abduction 4+ on the left; brisk reflexes in the arms; Lhermitte&apos;s sign present; gait and balance normal. Nine-hole peg test 24.5 seconds right, 31.0 seconds left. EDSS 2.0</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Warm and expressive; anxious; asks exact questions</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
